# Copy to `.env.static` and edit. Only read by `npm run build:static`.
#
# Vite loads `.env.<mode>` automatically, so `.env.static` is picked up by
# `vite build --mode static` and ignored by every other script.

# Public base path of the deploy.
#
# Leave as `/` for a root deploy (nginx, S3 website hosting, Netlify with no
# path prefix). For GitHub Pages project sites, set the repo name — the site is
# served from https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/, not the domain root:
#
#   VITE_BASE=/gpt2-from-scratch/
#
# Getting this wrong is silent locally: asset requests 404 only on the deployed
# subpath, which is why `src/lib/env.ts` routes every `public/` URL through one
# `publicPath()` helper.
VITE_BASE=/

# The backend origin. Normally left empty, because the bundled nginx.conf proxies
# `/api` to the backend and the browser stays same-origin — which also means no
# CORS setup and a WebSocket upgrade that just works.
#
# Set it only when the API is on a genuinely different origin. The scheme is
# rewritten for the WebSocket automatically (https -> wss), so give the https
# URL. If you do this, the backend must allow this origin:
# GPT2_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend-host
VITE_API_URL=
